Test Case ID: TC-DEV-03
Test Component: Project Scaffolding / Environment Configuration
Test Description: Verify that the project provides environment configuration templates (.env.example) and successfully loads local environment variables (.env) for backend/frontend execution.
(CodeSCR/TC-DEV-03.png)
Test Steps:
1.Inspect the project directory (backend / frontend) to check for the presence of an .env.example template file.
2.Create a local .env file based on the template structure.
3.Start the application servers and verify they successfully parse and utilize the defined environment variables (such as custom port numbers or database connection strings).
Expected Result: The application successfully reads variables from the environment file without throwing configuration or missing secret errors during startup.
Actual Result: Environment configuration templates were present in both modules, and local .env files were successfully read by the application servers upon launch.
Status: PASS ✅
